# Cursor Rules — Mestia

Cross-platform (desktop + Android) video downloader & media library.

## Stack
- Backend: Rust + Tauri v2 (`src-tauri/`)
- Frontend: React 18 + TypeScript + Vite 6 (`src/`)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS v4
- Animation: framer-motion (global `<MotionConfig reducedMotion="user">`; motion-animated elements use `.mestia-anim` to avoid clashing with the global CSS transform/opacity transition)
- i18n: custom lightweight context (no deps) — `src/lib/i18n.ts` (ru/en/zh dictionary + `t()`) + `src/context/LanguageContext.tsx` (`useI18n().t`); language in setting `lang`, OS-locale default
- DB: SQLite via tauri-plugin-sql (`src-tauri/migrations/`)
- Sidecars: yt-dlp + ffmpeg/ffprobe (`src-tauri/binaries/`)
- Android: Tauri mobile + youtubedl-android (GPL-3.0) via Kotlin plugin `MestiaPlugin` (`src-tauri/gen/android/`); desktop-only Rust gated by `#[cfg(desktop)]`, UI by `IS_ANDROID` (`src/lib/platform.ts`)
- Package manager: npm

## Commands
- Install: `npm install`
- Fetch binaries: `npm run fetch-binaries`
- Dev: `npm run tauri dev` (frontend only: `npm run dev`)
- Build + typecheck: `npm run build` (`tsc --noEmit && vite build`)
- Build installers: `npm run tauri build`
- Android: `npm run tauri android dev` / `npm run tauri android build -- --apk` (needs `ANDROID_HOME`, `NDK_HOME`)
- Tests: `npm test` (Vitest, frontend), `cargo test` (Rust). No linter; typecheck via `tsc --noEmit`.

## Architecture
- `src/context/` — ThemeContext, LanguageContext (i18n), DownloadsContext (queue/events), DragContext, LanContext (LAN peers/transfers/room)
- `src/components/` — Sidebar, Settings, DownloadsPanel, Splash, Toast, LibraryPicker, SendToDevice, etc.
- `src/lib/` — ipc.ts (bridge to Rust), db.ts (SQLite), i18n.ts (ru/en/zh dictionary + t()), platform.ts (IS_ANDROID), appIcon.ts (logo marks + theme-coloured favicon/window/tray/Android launcher icon), roomSync.ts (watch-together drift), media.ts (player src / media session / playback keep-alive)
- `src/views/` — Downloader, Locker (library), History, Player, MiniPlayer, Nearby (LAN), Room (watch together + queue)
- `src-tauri/src/` — lib.rs (plugins/tray/commands), downloader.rs (yt-dlp args/events), engine.rs (yt-dlp runner: sidecar / Android plugin), mobile.rs (Android bridge), storage.rs (files/watcher/thumbnails), lan.rs (LAN discovery/server/transfers/room), media.rs (Android loopback media server)
- `src-tauri/gen/android/` — Android project: MestiaPlugin.kt, DownloadService.kt, PlaybackService.kt, MainActivity.kt, manifest, Gradle deps
- `flatpak/` — Flatpak packaging for Steam Deck/SteamOS (manifest + desktop/metainfo); wraps the built .deb in the GNOME runtime, built in CI.
- `design/logo/` — logo concept SVGs + concepts.png; not part of the build.
- `docs/` — GitHub Pages landing site (self-contained index.html, all 8 themes + download links); static, not part of the app build.
- Frontend ↔ Rust via `src/lib/ipc.ts`.

## Token-saving rules
- Do NOT rewrite whole files. Edit only relevant lines; use `// ... existing code ...` markers.
- Be terse: no preamble, no flattery, answer directly.
- Read only the needed section of a file, not the whole file.
- Match surrounding code style (naming, comments, idioms).
- No unsolicited refactors — change only what was asked.
- Code comments are in Russian (match existing codebase). UI strings go through i18n — add a key to `src/lib/i18n.ts` (ru/en/zh) and render via `useI18n().t()`; never hardcode user-facing text.
- Keep `package.json` and `src-tauri/tauri.conf.json` versions in sync.

## Keep docs current
Update these docs in the SAME change that makes them wrong:
- New/removed/renamed folder or key module → update architecture map in `CLAUDE.md`, `.cursorrules`, `.context/index.md`.
- Changed `package.json` scripts → update Commands in `CLAUDE.md` and `.cursorrules`.
- Changed stack (new defining dependency: test runner, linter, state lib…) → update Stack in all three.
- Changed a core flow (download/library/auto-update) → update `.context/index.md`.
No structure/command/stack/flow change ⇒ no doc edit. Edit only wrong lines, don't rewrite.
